    <h2 id="faqs" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-12">9. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6 mt-6">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Do freelancers pay income tax in Singapore?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Yes. Freelancers, sole proprietors, private hire drivers, and gig workers are considered self-employed persons by IRAS. You must declare your Net Trade Income and pay progressive income taxes if your total taxable income (including employment and trade) exceeds S$22,000 annually, or if your net trade income exceeds S$6,000 requiring CPF Medisave contributions.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How is Net Trade Income calculated for self-employed persons?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Net Trade Income equals Gross Business Revenue minus allowable business expenses and allowable capital allowances. It represents the actual profit you made from your self-employed endeavors.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the simplified expense deduction for drivers?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Private hire drivers (Grab, Gojek, etc.) and taxi drivers can claim a fixed 60% of their gross driving fares as deemed business expenses. This means you do not need to keep detailed receipts for fuel, maintenance, or rental. You only pay tax on the remaining 40% of your gross income.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Do I need to pay CPF as a freelancer in Singapore?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">While contributions to the CPF Ordinary Account and Special Account are voluntary, you are legally required to make mandatory MediSave contributions if your Net Trade Income for the year exceeds S$6,000.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How long must I keep my business receipts and records?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">You are legally mandated to retain all business records, invoices, and expense receipts for at least 5 years from the relevant Year of Assessment, in case IRAS requests them for verification.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

